np.float64 is a Python float subclass : True
np.float32 is a Python float subclass : False
np.int64   is a Python int   subclass : False
np.bool_   is a Python bool  subclass : False

=> A-23 _require_real uses isinstance(value,(int,float)), so the declared
   type discipline ALREADY admits np.float64 while rejecting np.float32.
   The float32/float64 hazard it exists to prevent is therefore already
   half-open at the only place it is enforced.
   NumericalConfig.create(min_sigma=float64) -> ACCEPT, stored 5.0 (float64)
   NumericalConfig.create(min_sigma=float32) -> reject(NumericalConfigError)
   NumericalConfig.create(min_sigma=bool_) -> reject(NumericalConfigError)
